{"metadata":{"name":"Sunan an Nasai","section":{"21":{"eng-name":"The Book of Funerals","ara-name":"كتاب الجنائز"}},"section_detail":{"21":{"hadithnumber_first":1818,"hadithnumber_last":2089,"arabicnumber_first":1818,"arabicnumber_last":2089}}},"hadiths":[{"hadithnumber":1842,"arabicnumber":1842,"text":"Rapporté par Jabir : \"Mon père a été amené le jour de Uhud, il avait été mutilé. Il a été placé devant le Messager d’Allah ﷺ, recouvert d’un tissu. Je voulais le découvrir mais ma famille me l’a interdit","grades":[{"name":"Abu Ghuddah","grade":"Sahih"},{"name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Sahih - Agreed Upon"}],"reference":{"book":21,"hadith":25},"chapter":{"id":12,"ara-name":"باب تَسْجِيَةِ الْمَيِّتِ ","eng-name":"Covering the Deceased","isFirstHadith":true}}]}